{"uid":"e5ff99133f8f1965","name":"test_a_real_agent_uid_probe_cannot_plant_or_replace_the_protected_hooks_entry","fullName":"tests.test_commit_scan_engine_boundary#test_a_real_agent_uid_probe_cannot_plant_or_replace_the_protected_hooks_entry","historyId":"d71b394e6c812c514a649af281f20501","time":{"start":1791935079423,"stop":1791935079424,"duration":1},"description":"Task cure-01-02, requirement I.1/DoD 9: a real uid-boundary probe of\n    the containing path, in THIS process, at the agent uid -- no container\n    needed, because `privsep.commit_scan_hooks_dir()`'s parent\n    (`/var/lib/ralphd`) is already root-owned wherever the engine's uid\n    boundary exists, including the job container this suite runs in.\n\n    It proves the half of the finding that mode bits cannot: the\n    `commit-scan-hooks` directory ENTRY itself (and any name beside it)\n    cannot be created, written, renamed or chmod-ed from the agent uid,\n    while listing the parent -- which the agent-uid hook process needs in\n    order to reach the hook at all -- still succeeds. The installed hook\n    file's own denial, which needs the hooks directory to have actually been\n    installed by an elevated engine, is\n    `tests/test_commit_scan_hooks_docker.py`'s real-container probe.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task cure-01-02, requirement I.1/DoD 9: a real uid-boundary probe of<br />\nthe containing path, in THIS process, at the agent uid -- no container<br />\nneeded, because <code>privsep.commit_scan_hooks_dir()</code>'s parent<br />\n(<code>/var/lib/ralphd</code>) is already root-owned wherever the engine's uid<br />\nboundary exists, including the job container this suite runs in.</p>\n<pre><code>It proves the half of the finding that mode bits cannot: the\n`commit-scan-hooks` directory ENTRY itself (and any name beside it)\ncannot be created, written, renamed or chmod-ed from the agent uid,\nwhile listing the parent -- which the agent-uid hook process needs in\norder to reach the hook at all -- 